It is given that
<span class="math display">\[\begin{equation*}
    x_2 = \frac{1}{1 - x_1}, \quad x_3 = \frac{1}{1 - x_2}, \quad x_4 = \frac{1}{1 - x_3}, \quad\text{where $x_1 \ne 0$ or $1$.}
\end{equation*}\]</span>
<p>Prove that (i) <span class="math inline">\(x_1x_2x_3 + 1 = 0\)</span>, (ii) <span class="math inline">\(x_4 = x_1\)</span>.</p>
